cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "STL-Dev-MPI: pyramidal scattering-covariance statistics, gradients and synthesis on HEALPix and 2D grids, in Rust with MPI and CUDA"
abstract: >-
  STL-Dev-MPI computes the scattering-covariance statistics (mean, variance,
  S1, S2, S3, S4) of full-sky HEALPix maps, disc patches and periodic images,
  together with their exact gradient, and synthesises maps whose statistics
  match those of a target map or of a population of maps. The statistics and
  their gradient are computed block by block over the multiresolution pyramid
  with explicit vector-Jacobian products, and the sky is split between MPI
  ranks or GPUs, so that the memory of a process is bounded by its share of
  the sky. It is the high-performance port of the patch-local engine of
  STL-Dev and matches its statistics to 1e-10. Python bindings expose the
  engines and their gradients to NumPy and PyTorch.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/jmdelouis/STL-Dev-MPI"
version: "0.1.0"
